      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1368706220,
      "text": "Cadaba farinosa is a 2–8 m (6.6–26.2 ft) high evergreen shrub or small tree that belongs to the caper family. It has simple ovate leaves with entire margins, zygomorphic, spidery, greenish, yellowish, whitish or pinkish flowers, and is covered in powdery hairs or scales, particularly the younger parts. It can be found in a zone from Senegal to India between the desert and the savanna."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Cadaba farinosa",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cadaba_farinosa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 207931652,
      "text": "Cadaba farinosa est un arbuste qui peut atteindre 5 m de haut et au feuillage persistant de la famille des Capparacées."
    }
  },
